ummary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What version of Next.js are you using?\n\n11.1.0\n\n### What version of Node.js are you using?\n\n16.6.2\n\n### What browser are you using?\n\nChrome\n\n### What operating system are you using?\n\nmacOS\n\n### How are you deploying your application?\n\nyarn run dev\n\n### Describe the Bug\n\nRendering a link on the **Unhandled Runtime Error** page error, which mixed an **Open** character that shouldn't exist. (See Pic)\r\n\r\n![1](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/66008528/129474194-06775712-0318-49ca-af1b-fac57cffd65a.png)\r\n![2](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/66008528/129474196-cf011193-d457-4e67-bd0a-9e3cc6cab23f.png)\r\n![3](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/66008528/129474198-d2837401-ebf3-42e1-8b47-3d39ccf93fde.png)\r\n\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nAdd a full stop(.) after the link to distinguish between link and text or restructure that sentence on [GitHub](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/971b17f1e912b8ab69b9ac7cb83617875a2b3d86/packages/next/client/link.tsx#L238) to make that [link](https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/link-multiple-children) works.\r\n\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```\r\nimport Link from 'next/link';\r\n\r\nconst PretendToBeWrong = () => {\r\n    return (\r\n        <div>\r\n            <Link href='example.com'>\r\n              <div></div>\r\n              <div></div>\r\n            </Link>\r\n        </div>\r\n    );\r\n};\r\n\r\nexport default PretendToBeWrong;\r\n```","closed_by":{"login":"kodiakhq[bot]","id":49736102,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk3MzYxMDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29196?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/kodiakhq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodiakhq%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users